{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791828641,"nonce":"/oGrEx10oSpLwHZ9K8gGhI5/SZ8=","title":"Reveal keyboard selection in CommandList","message":"Command changes its active signal for ArrowUp/ArrowDown/Home/End but does not reveal the selected CommandItem in its scrolling CommandList. With a grouped catalog taller than the list's max-height, End highlights the last result below the viewport while focus stays in CommandInput.\n\nChimpMonk's editor command center currently observes active/query and reveals the result using ashui.input.Scroll after row layout. Its WorkspaceSnapshot checks End, Home and filtering and captures the visible result. This behavior belongs in Command so other users do not need a layout hook.\n\nReveal only when the active selection or filter changes, preserve manual scrolling between changes, and remove observers with the owner. Verify arrow navigation, Home/End, filtering, selected row removal and closing/disposal while scrolled.","files":null}]}